// GENERATED by scripts/build/gen_settings.py from dll_cs/settings/*.cs (ageofai.ini's keys) - not edited by hand:
// a setting is a field there (dll_cs/settings/settings.cs: the format), config/ageofai.ini is made of them too.
// generated: rows.h baeeac046c84cbec, ageofai.ini 92f989ec7a9769c4
// THE SETTINGS: the keys of ageofai.ini (and the test ini's own), one row each - its kind, section, key, default and
// the kind's limits - in the shipped file's order. settings.c makes the rows g_set (g_set.lead_targets: the value in
// force), read once when the DLL loads; what a setting means is told in config/ageofai.ini above its key (the file is the
// documentation, the rows are what the code knows). Both are made of dll_cs/settings/*.cs - a new setting is a field
// there (scripts/build/settings_check.py, run by the build, still holds the two together).
//
//   FLAG    0 or 1
//   INT     a whole number lo .. hi (outside: a warning, the value used)
//   LIMIT   a whole number lo .. hi and nothing else (outside: a mistake, the default)
//   NUM     any whole number (a level, a bit mask, a count: what the code makes of it is its own)
//   SHARE   a share, a float (home_guard_share=35% -> 0.35), lo% .. hi%; the default in percent (a part that keeps
//           whole percents: setting_pct(g_set_ai[1].navy_share) -> 25)
//   CHOICE  one of the names in lo ("auto,d3d,gdi"), kept as its index (auto 0, d3d 1 ...); the default by name
//   STR     a text, shorter than lo characters (the buffer's size)
//   STR_P   a text per player slot: the keys key0 .. key15 (personality_P2)
//   FACTOR  a multiplier, a float (friendly_collision=75% -> 0.75), lo% .. hi%; its 1 the game's own
//   FLAGS   named fields in one key, lo their list (OVERLAY_FIELDS below): field_bool(name) on or off,
//           field_enum(name, "a/b/c") one of its names, kept as its index (a 0); the code reads
//           g_set.key.name. In the file words apart by commas or spaces: a bool by its name (on) or
//           name=0 / name=1, an enum name=b, all: every bool on, none or empty: every field its first; the
//           default the same way. A part that keeps a bit mask: SETTING_BITS(g_set_ai[1].army_plan) - field i, bit i.
//
// A range (INT, SHARE) is a sanity bound, not a limit the code relies on: a value outside it is a warning in the log
// ("- used anyway") and the value kept (formation_wait=0% is silly but runs). A mistake is only what can't be used at
// all - no number, no whole number, a FLAG not 0 or 1, no CHOICE's name, a text too long: "- the default instead". A
// range the code would break beyond is no range: the code clamps (draw_limit, the sound channels do).
//
// A key's name is its own across the file: no two sections have the same key (gen_settings.py stops the build), so a
// section is only where the key stands in the file and its page in ageofai_config.exe - a key moved keeps its name.
// X: a row of any section but [ai_base] (the test ini's [autotest] too, which exists only there) - g_set.key. D: a row of [ai_base], one value
// per AI difficulty - g_set_ai[d].key (0 easy, 1 medium, 2 hard), each from [ai_easy] / [ai_hard], else [ai_base] (medium plays
// [ai_base] itself); a part that doesn't tell the difficulties apart reads [1], the medium one. The test ini's [autotest] overrides any
// row by that same name (lead_targets=0, present=gdi, llm_enabled=1, avoid_towers=0 - every difficulty).

